{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-22 08:10:05 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-22 15:10:05 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a0bacb-3b91-7190-8412-3f1e85bb552a\n\nB1 SIGNED OFF  \nB3 SIGNED OFF\n\nThe host-capability corrections are accurate and require no design change.\nThe current design correctly records char, ratio, and bigint as JVM-only.\nOn ClojureDart, a genuinely distinguishable `:char` class is unavailable;\none-codepoint values are therefore treated as strings, while unsupported ratio\nand bigint classes are refused.\n\nBuilding B3 before B2 is architecturally sound. Section 6 explicitly permits\nthe shortest-path ordering to proceed B0, B1, B2, B6, then B3-B5, but B3 and\nB2 share only the already-frozen instruction shapes. B3’s standalone\nhand-built-vector tests do not create a dependency on B1 or B2.\n\nI found no violation of D1-D16, the invariant set, or the must-not-change\nlists:\n\n- B1 derives its opcode table from `vector-operand-table`, defines the\n  descriptor and lowering version, preserves exact scalar bytes, computes H\n  through one function, and rejects conflicting body-scope declarations.\n- B1’s validator rejects malformed structure, invalid targets, and invalid\n  bound references; its host-support refusal remains an explicit later\n  receive/load check.\n- B3 keeps frames outermost-first while resolving depth zero from the\n  innermost frame, captures persistent frame stacks in closures, preserves\n  named `resolve-var` ordering, and adds no protocol methods.\n- B3 deliberately leaves `environment` unsupported until the lift exists and\n  keeps effects, continuations, parking, and resume for B4.\n- B3’s direct construction before B1/B2 is acceptable because B1 is the\n  sole image-admission boundary for the eventual integrated path.\n\nThe next coherent unit is B2, the named-datom lowerer. Its scope remains as\nwritten: adapt `linearize/lower`, reconstruct lexical context from the image,\nrewrite variable and closure operands, validate through B1, and prove the lift\nround trip. B1’s actual implementation strengthens that plan by providing the\nstable validator, H function, golden fixtures, and host-domain checks that B2\nmust consume.\n\nOwner attention before merge:\n\n- Merge B1 and B3 as separate commits only when the owner is ready; their\n  independent branches and intentional lack of cross-file dependencies are\n  sound.\n- Preserve B1’s clarified host matrix, especially the distinction between\n  JVM `:char` and ClojureDart one-codepoint strings.\n- No additional architectural decision or blocking change is required before\n  starting B2."}}
